From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] metrics: correlate and deliver candidate RCPI response

An agent normally rests in topo_synchronized, not configured.  The
Unassociated STA result orchestrator only accepted configured, selected an
arbitrary first radio, and read the response entries from that radio's data
model instead of the command snapshot populated by the asynchronous OneWifi
callback.  Consequently every valid HAL result remained pending until the
command TTL expired.

Route a single-radio query and its asynchronous result by operating class,
preserve the parsed result explicitly when constructing the command snapshot,
allow the stable topo_synchronized state, serialize the response entries from
that snapshot, and send the fire-and-forget response synchronously while
preserving the radio's stable state.  Keep one query MID outstanding until the
metrics response arrives: an ACK accepts the request but does not complete the
measurement, and a timeout clears the transaction so it cannot poison later
queries.  A client-capability exchange may leave a controller radio in the
confirmed state, which is also a valid starting point for this independent
measurement transaction.

